# channelswap

- Label: Channel Swap
- Category: Copernicus (`Cop`), Houdini 22.0.368
- Inputs: 0 to 3
- Parameters: 14 (exact, read from Houdini by hython)
- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/channelswap.html
- Summary (EN): Rearranges the channels within one multichannel layer, VDB or attribute, for example RGB to BGR. It can also copy a channel from a second input, or set a channel to Zero, One or a constant Value.
- Résumé (FR) : Le nœud channelswap réordonne ou remplace les canaux d'une même couche multicanale, par exemple du RGB vers du BGR.

- Inputs meaning: ["channels: the layer, VDB or attribute whose channels are swapped", "alternate: the layer, VDB or attribute to take channels from", "mask (optional): per-pixel mask, scaled by the Mask parameter"]

- Key parameters: [{"name": "Signature", "meaning": "Layer type the input accepts"}, {"name": "Mask", "meaning": "How much of the new value is mixed in; default 1 uses only the new value"}, {"name": "Source for Red / Green / Blue / Alpha", "meaning": "First Input or Second Input, then Red, Green, Blue, Alpha, Zero, One or Value; defaults map each channel to itself"}, {"name": "Value for Red / Green / Blue / Alpha", "meaning": "Constant used when that channel's source is Value"}]

- Caveats: ["A channel that does not exist in the input follows the standard channel extension rules", "For complex workflows, the page suggests Channel Split and Channel Join; Channel Swap creates fewer intermediate buffers"]

